1
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:04,971
MICHIKO DAIMON, FREELANCE SURGEON

2
00:00:08,942 --> 00:00:12,278
Wait right there, let me cut it.

3
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:26,760
Beef after surgery is the best.

4
00:00:27,961 --> 00:00:33,333
I'm in love. I've fallen in love.
Your use of the scalpel...

5
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,503
Your healthy appetite
after a hard operation...

6
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:40,106
And your strong mentality
that cares for no one...

7
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:44,044
You're the woman
whom I've long searched for.

8
00:00:44,944 --> 00:00:47,781
Will you be my partner?

9
00:00:48,915 --> 00:00:50,116
To our future.

10
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:55,155
Director Fujikawa,

11
00:00:55,622 --> 00:00:59,426
thank you for inviting
someone like me as well.

12
00:00:59,492 --> 00:01:01,661
Of course I'll invite you.

13
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:04,597
Dr. Daimon can't be without you.

14
00:01:04,998 --> 00:01:08,234
Oh yeah, I have
a gift for you, Mr. Kanbara.

15
00:01:08,802 --> 00:01:10,537
A special one-of-a-kind tie.

16
00:01:10,870 --> 00:01:13,073
The only one in the world.

17
00:01:15,275 --> 00:01:16,443
Well, I can't wait.

18
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:20,780
How nice.

19
00:01:21,948 --> 00:01:25,285
I love this design.

20
00:01:31,124 --> 00:01:32,459
I have to answer this.

21
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:35,261
What?

22
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:36,563
It's trouble.

23
00:01:37,564 --> 00:01:39,866
Ms. Tokachi has been admitted.

24
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:42,936
She'd like to decide on a surgery date.

25
00:01:43,002 --> 00:01:44,504
Please return now.

26
00:01:44,571 --> 00:01:47,273
I'm entertaining important guests.

27
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:48,875
I can't go back,

28
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:50,310
so have Achi do it.

29
00:01:50,376 --> 00:01:51,377
What?

30
00:01:55,014 --> 00:01:57,951
She's a soon-to-be minister.

31
00:01:58,017 --> 00:01:59,319
I'm hanging up.

32
00:02:00,019 --> 00:02:01,321
Director Fujikawa!

33
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:21,474
Michiko, you really have the best manager.

34
00:02:22,041 --> 00:02:24,644
With such a great treasurer,

35
00:02:24,711 --> 00:02:27,747
you're all set for your retirement.

36
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:29,749
- Huh?
- Even now...

37
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:32,085
You must have made this much.

38
00:02:32,418 --> 00:02:33,486
200 thousand yen?

39
00:02:33,553 --> 00:02:35,555
You must be joking.

40
00:02:35,622 --> 00:02:37,490
Add 3 more zeros.

41
00:02:40,793 --> 00:02:41,661
200 million yen?

42
00:02:42,729 --> 00:02:46,065
It's not like I won the lottery.

43
00:02:46,132 --> 00:02:49,435
Director Fujikawa,
your jokes are hilarious.

44
00:02:50,603 --> 00:02:53,907
200 million? No way.

45
00:02:59,212 --> 00:03:00,079
The Head Nurse.

46
00:03:00,146 --> 00:03:01,347
The Head Nurse.

47
00:03:01,414 --> 00:03:03,349
JUNKO SHIRAKI, HEAD NURSE

48
00:03:03,416 --> 00:03:05,084
Karaoke alone...

49
00:03:06,119 --> 00:03:08,855
I feel the intensity and sorrow of a woman

50
00:03:08,922 --> 00:03:12,025
who has lived a life of nursing.

51
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:14,994
Let's forget we saw that.

52
00:03:21,968 --> 00:03:25,672
This is a story about
a maverick female doctor.

53
00:03:28,608 --> 00:03:33,646
Mr. Tendo will be making his rounds.

54
00:03:34,581 --> 00:03:39,452
<i>In 2014, medical establishments</i>
<i>collapsed and became more corrupt.</i>

55
00:03:39,519 --> 00:03:41,754
<i>Medicine, which handles lives,</i>

56
00:03:42,188 --> 00:03:45,625
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

57
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:48,661
<i>However, despite these conditions,</i>

58
00:03:48,995 --> 00:03:53,032
<i>Japan announced to export</i>
<i>state of the art medical services</i>

59
00:03:53,099 --> 00:03:55,935
<i>as a growth strategy.</i>

60
00:03:56,002 --> 00:04:00,373
<i>Healthcare entered an era</i>
<i>of the strong preying on the weak.</i>

61
00:04:01,574 --> 00:04:05,812
<i>Then came freelance doctors</i>
<i>who don't belong to hospitals.</i>

62
00:04:06,179 --> 00:04:09,515
<i>In other words, maverick doctors.</i>

63
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:10,917
Let's get steak again.

64
00:04:10,984 --> 00:04:12,252
Steak, yes.

65
00:04:13,052 --> 00:04:14,087
Hear that?

66
00:04:14,153 --> 00:04:15,421
Since when are

67
00:04:15,488 --> 00:04:16,756
he and Demon like that?

68
00:04:16,823 --> 00:04:17,824
Like what?

69
00:04:17,890 --> 00:04:19,559
TAKASHI EBINA, SURGICAL DIRECTOR

70
00:04:19,626 --> 00:04:20,627
You mean like that?

71
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,301
Seriously?

72
00:04:28,368 --> 00:04:31,137
Dr. Daimon, Is something wrong?

73
00:04:31,204 --> 00:04:32,639
You're a doctor?

74
00:04:34,974 --> 00:04:36,743
Quiet!

75
00:04:37,377 --> 00:04:39,112
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

76
00:04:39,746 --> 00:04:43,383
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

77
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:47,820
<i>Her medical license</i>
<i>and experience are her only weapons.</i>

78
00:04:49,355 --> 00:04:51,457
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

79
00:04:51,924 --> 00:04:54,894
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

80
00:05:16,049 --> 00:05:17,383
Thank you.

81
00:05:17,450 --> 00:05:18,618
Please rest assured.

82
00:05:19,252 --> 00:05:22,989
Our hospital will do everything
in our power to cure you.

83
00:05:23,690 --> 00:05:25,158
Please.

84
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:34,067
Please accept this.

85
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:40,873
SHOZO ACHI, SURGEON

86
00:05:42,942 --> 00:05:45,812
I will begin the preoperative conference.

87
00:05:46,479 --> 00:05:49,849
Ms. Yoshiko Tokachi, 55 years old.

88
00:05:49,916 --> 00:05:55,588
Inferior myocardial infarction
and hepatocellular carcinoma stage IVa.

89
00:06:00,393 --> 00:06:02,061
As you all know,

90
00:06:02,762 --> 00:06:04,797
Ms. Tokachi is a Diet member,

91
00:06:05,331 --> 00:06:08,167
and is important to our country.

92
00:06:08,234 --> 00:06:13,706
A special team to cure
Ms. Tokachi will be established.

93
00:06:14,407 --> 00:06:15,641
The team's leader is

94
00:06:16,075 --> 00:06:19,178
Surgical Department Director Fujikawa.

95
00:06:20,279 --> 00:06:21,848
Dr. Fujikawa, please.

96
00:06:29,655 --> 00:06:33,159
Her left coronary artery is occluded.

97
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:36,162
Necrosis of myocardial cells.

98
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:38,431
It's serious heart failure.

99
00:06:38,498 --> 00:06:40,500
The possible methods

100
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:44,170
are heart transplant
or an artificial heart.

101
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:47,640
And on the liver,

102
00:06:47,707 --> 00:06:49,776
a massive 13cm tumor can be confirmed.

103
00:06:49,842 --> 00:06:50,977
Your plans?

104
00:06:51,043 --> 00:06:55,815
I will approach this
with a world's first method.

105
00:06:56,349 --> 00:06:57,183
What?

106
00:06:57,250 --> 00:07:01,220
For the heart failure, Fujikawa Method.

107
00:07:01,287 --> 00:07:03,756
Myocardial regeneration

108
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:10,129
with autologous myoblast sheet,
which I've been working on.

109
00:07:13,499 --> 00:07:14,700
Regeneration...

110
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:16,169
And the liver?

111
00:07:16,803 --> 00:07:19,105
The tumor is too large,

112
00:07:19,172 --> 00:07:21,474
and at most, 20%

113
00:07:21,541 --> 00:07:23,342
can be retained.

114
00:07:23,409 --> 00:07:24,677
The Fujikawa Method,

115
00:07:24,744 --> 00:07:30,983
total right hepatic and partial left
hepatic lobectomy will cure her.

116
00:07:31,050 --> 00:07:32,084
Hold on.

117
00:07:32,552 --> 00:07:36,122
Much blood loss can be expected.

118
00:07:36,189 --> 00:07:38,224
How will you counter that?

119
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:41,194
I will cool her down to hypothermia,

120
00:07:41,661 --> 00:07:46,165
and use a cardiopulmonary bypass
to stop circulation

121
00:07:46,666 --> 00:07:49,802
to prevent brain damage and blood loss.

122
00:07:49,869 --> 00:07:52,138
If under 20% of the liver remains,

123
00:07:52,205 --> 00:07:53,706
regeneration is tough.

124
00:07:54,774 --> 00:07:56,309
It's too hard.

125
00:07:56,375 --> 00:07:57,376
Exactly!

126
00:07:57,977 --> 00:07:59,779
Because it is hard,

127
00:07:59,846 --> 00:08:02,748
if we succeed with the 2 methods at once,

128
00:08:03,082 --> 00:08:05,218
it will be a world's first case.

129
00:08:05,284 --> 00:08:08,287
This operative method
will shock the world.

130
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:13,226
Is it possible?

131
00:08:13,292 --> 00:08:16,929
We will approach it with a team.
It's fine.

132
00:08:16,996 --> 00:08:18,264
And the liver?

133
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:19,432
I will ask...

134
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,369
Dr. Daimon to do that.

135
00:08:25,571 --> 00:08:26,706
I won't do that.

136
00:08:26,772 --> 00:08:27,940
What?

137
00:08:28,441 --> 00:08:32,378
I registered you as a member of the team.

138
00:08:33,279 --> 00:08:34,714
You cannot refuse.

139
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:35,815
I won't do that.

140
00:08:38,584 --> 00:08:40,620
Why are you refusing
a world's first surgery

141
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:45,691
when your hobby is surgery?

142
00:08:45,758 --> 00:08:46,792
Don't feel like it.

143
00:08:49,228 --> 00:08:53,766
My contract says I won't help
with promotions or manuscripts.

144
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:57,236
That's why I won't do that.

145
00:08:59,171 --> 00:09:00,206
Dr. Daimon!

146
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:03,442
I will not forgive you today.

147
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:07,079
How dare you
act like that towards Mr. Tendo.

148
00:09:09,849 --> 00:09:11,350
Head Nurse Shiraki.

149
00:09:11,851 --> 00:09:12,718
Yes.

150
00:09:15,488 --> 00:09:20,893
Please give your full support
for the world's first surgery.

151
00:09:24,163 --> 00:09:25,097
Yes, sir.

152
00:09:26,599 --> 00:09:28,467
I'm counting on you.

153
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:30,937
I'm very grateful.

154
00:09:32,204 --> 00:09:34,774
Mr. Tendo... Yes, sir!

155
00:09:35,207 --> 00:09:36,175
Yes, sir!

156
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,415
Seriously?

157
00:09:44,317 --> 00:09:45,451
You love him?

158
00:09:47,553 --> 00:09:48,521
You do...

159
00:09:51,490 --> 00:09:52,625
Dr. Fujikawa.

160
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:57,396
- We need to talk.
- Yes, sir.

161
00:09:58,197 --> 00:10:02,034
- Move.
- Daimon!

162
00:10:02,101 --> 00:10:05,004
Good job refusing today.

163
00:10:05,071 --> 00:10:06,872
You're one of us.

164
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:07,807
Have a tangerine...

165
00:10:08,541 --> 00:10:12,211
So you remembered
our bond from the 3rd Branch Hospital.

166
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,213
- Who are you?
- Hara Mamoru.

167
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,148
- Never mind.
- Have a tangerine.

168
00:10:16,215 --> 00:10:19,251
Let's forget about the past.
We will welcome you.

169
00:10:19,719 --> 00:10:21,387
Your smile's scary too.

170
00:10:21,887 --> 00:10:24,890
I won't help with faction battles.

171
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:26,692
Daimon.

172
00:10:26,759 --> 00:10:28,661
- Don't say that.
- Tangerines...

173
00:10:28,728 --> 00:10:31,430
He charges crazy surgery fees,

174
00:10:31,497 --> 00:10:33,766
but his office is really lame.

175
00:10:33,833 --> 00:10:38,037
That manager's embezzling quite a bit.

176
00:10:38,904 --> 00:10:40,706
I'll cut some melon.

177
00:10:40,773 --> 00:10:44,443
No, thank you. I heard
the melon here is expensive.

178
00:10:44,510 --> 00:10:46,345
- Don't trouble yourself.
- Are you sure?

179
00:10:47,613 --> 00:10:49,281
Michiko's late.

180
00:10:49,348 --> 00:10:52,918
I must have you
persuade her no matter what.

181
00:10:52,985 --> 00:10:57,490
Is the deposit money
I put under that tie not enough?

182
00:10:57,556 --> 00:10:59,458
Well...

183
00:10:59,525 --> 00:11:00,593
Fine.

184
00:11:01,594 --> 00:11:03,095
Then take this too.

185
00:11:03,529 --> 00:11:05,998
Oh my. Please take him for a second.

186
00:11:07,433 --> 00:11:08,334
Ouch...

187
00:11:09,402 --> 00:11:11,270
Useless cat! Go to hell!

188
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:16,776
Not you, I was talking to the cat.

189
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:21,647
So please make sure
Ms. Daimon becomes my 1st assistant.

190
00:11:21,714 --> 00:11:23,983
Have a nice day.

191
00:11:24,984 --> 00:11:27,219
Are you alright, Ben Casey?

192
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,188
Did you get hurt?

193
00:11:30,222 --> 00:11:31,290
How terrible.

194
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:33,659
I saw his true colors.

195
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:37,630
Ouch...

196
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:41,200
Ouch...

197
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:50,509
- I'm home.
- Hey.

198
00:11:50,576 --> 00:11:51,911
Where's Akira?

199
00:11:51,977 --> 00:11:54,380
He said he has a stomach ache.

200
00:11:54,914 --> 00:11:56,716
I bet he ate something.

201
00:11:56,782 --> 00:11:57,650
Really?

202
00:11:58,017 --> 00:11:59,652
- Good night.
- Fine

203
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:03,489
Akira, are you alright?

204
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:05,157
It still hurts.

205
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:06,459
Are you okay?

206
00:12:06,525 --> 00:12:08,661
I'm still in pain.

207
00:12:12,865 --> 00:12:15,101
Look. I'm better now.

208
00:12:15,167 --> 00:12:16,469
I'm fine

209
00:12:16,535 --> 00:12:17,436
Hold on.

210
00:12:17,503 --> 00:12:19,171
Let me check...

211
00:12:19,739 --> 00:12:21,373
I have myocardial infarction

212
00:12:22,274 --> 00:12:25,845
and a liver tumor.

213
00:12:27,279 --> 00:12:30,516
Every hospital said surgery is impossible.

214
00:12:32,318 --> 00:12:34,854
However, this great doctor

215
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:37,089
has promised to cure me

216
00:12:37,156 --> 00:12:40,926
with the latest operative method.

217
00:12:41,393 --> 00:12:44,630
I am Fujikawa of
the Advanced Medical Care Center.

218
00:12:46,132 --> 00:12:47,166
Please rest assured.

219
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:50,603
I will cure her with my Fujikawa Method.

220
00:12:53,672 --> 00:12:54,707
Dr. Fujikawa...

221
00:12:56,909 --> 00:13:00,579
In order for that,
the Advanced Medical Care Center

222
00:13:01,147 --> 00:13:03,949
has established
a team to cure Ms. Tokachi.

223
00:13:04,850 --> 00:13:09,588
We will fully utilize the hospital's
resources for Ms. Tokachi.

224
00:13:09,655 --> 00:13:10,923
Hurry up.

225
00:13:10,990 --> 00:13:15,327
You have to be there for this.

226
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:16,929
I'm sorry.

227
00:13:18,597 --> 00:13:19,932
- Look at you.
- Stop.

228
00:13:19,999 --> 00:13:20,833
Please hurry.

229
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:21,934
Come on.

230
00:13:22,001 --> 00:13:23,502
- Dress properly.
- Hurry up.

231
00:13:23,569 --> 00:13:27,640
- She's fine now. Sorry for the wait.
- Will Ms. Tokachi's care team

232
00:13:27,706 --> 00:13:29,208
please smile?

233
00:13:29,275 --> 00:13:30,242
I won't do that.

234
00:13:30,943 --> 00:13:32,511
I won't...

235
00:13:33,345 --> 00:13:35,381
What's with you? I won't do that!

236
00:13:35,447 --> 00:13:37,016
I refused.

237
00:13:37,883 --> 00:13:39,985
I won't be his assistant.

238
00:13:40,052 --> 00:13:42,655
Don't say that.

239
00:13:42,721 --> 00:13:45,991
Let's make the world's first

240
00:13:46,058 --> 00:13:48,427
Fujikawa Method a success.

241
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:50,663
I absolutely need your skills.

242
00:13:50,729 --> 00:13:51,997
It's 5pm. I'm leaving.

243
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:54,700
Dr. Daimon.

244
00:13:56,635 --> 00:14:01,240
You are merely a surgeon
who was hired with money.

245
00:14:02,775 --> 00:14:03,876
So?

246
00:14:03,943 --> 00:14:06,545
Why do you think we pay you

247
00:14:07,279 --> 00:14:11,116
a huge fee and give special treatment?

248
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:13,219
Huge fee? What?

249
00:14:13,285 --> 00:14:14,286
You don't know?

250
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:19,391
We pay a ridiculous fee every time.

251
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:24,964
I have an ideal form
of healthcare I'm aiming for.

252
00:14:25,931 --> 00:14:30,169
In order to realize this...
I'll do anything.

253
00:14:30,569 --> 00:14:31,403
And?

254
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:34,139
If you, who has no support behind you,

255
00:14:35,407 --> 00:14:37,543
go against my authority...

256
00:14:39,245 --> 00:14:43,449
You won't be able to operate
in any hospital in Japan.

257
00:14:45,184 --> 00:14:47,019
So you're threatening me?

258
00:14:49,755 --> 00:14:53,359
You know, everything you're saying...

259
00:14:53,759 --> 00:14:55,060
It sounds fake.

260
00:14:56,228 --> 00:14:57,296
How dare you!

261
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:02,801
Dr. Daimon, apologize.

262
00:15:03,736 --> 00:15:06,872
No matter how much you refuse,

263
00:15:07,473 --> 00:15:10,409
your manager already accepted for money.

264
00:15:11,844 --> 00:15:16,015
I've already paid Mr. Kanbara
a hefty deposit for the surgery.

265
00:15:16,615 --> 00:15:18,183
You don't even know that?

266
00:15:20,986 --> 00:15:22,021
Really?

267
00:15:26,158 --> 00:15:30,029
I pray the world's first
surgery will succeed.

268
00:15:35,401 --> 00:15:36,669
Dr. Daimon.

269
00:15:43,575 --> 00:15:44,610
Mr. Tendo.

270
00:15:45,744 --> 00:15:47,413
Happy birthday.

271
00:15:47,479 --> 00:15:49,782
It's a one-of-a-kind tie

272
00:15:49,848 --> 00:15:52,051
I had specially made for you.

273
00:15:52,117 --> 00:15:52,952
Birthday?

274
00:15:53,018 --> 00:15:55,321
Yes, that's right. For me?

275
00:15:57,489 --> 00:15:58,457
Thank you.

276
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,302
Why'd you accept?

277
00:16:10,369 --> 00:16:13,005
What's with the deposit for surgery?

278
00:16:13,505 --> 00:16:14,807
Welcome back.

279
00:16:14,873 --> 00:16:16,175
Everyone's waiting.

280
00:16:16,241 --> 00:16:18,410
Not now. Explain it to me.

281
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:21,146
You're not playing mahjong today?

282
00:16:26,352 --> 00:16:29,621
I'll never work with Tendo or Fujikawa.

283
00:16:29,688 --> 00:16:32,191
But it's in the evening paper.

284
00:16:35,127 --> 00:16:36,195
I won't do that.

285
00:16:36,261 --> 00:16:38,764
You look terrible in this.

286
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:41,133
Yeah, couldn't you have smiled?

287
00:16:42,568 --> 00:16:44,203
It's a good deal.

288
00:16:44,269 --> 00:16:46,238
If you save the next minister,

289
00:16:46,305 --> 00:16:48,107
there will be benefits.

290
00:16:48,173 --> 00:16:49,742
- Exactly.
- No.

291
00:16:50,576 --> 00:16:52,544
- I won't be Fujikawa's assistant.
- Why?

292
00:16:52,611 --> 00:16:54,213
His technique is sloppy.

293
00:16:54,713 --> 00:16:56,015
No way.

294
00:16:56,081 --> 00:16:59,685
For the stomach cancer before,
he was sloppy

295
00:16:59,752 --> 00:17:02,988
and Daimon ended up...

296
00:17:03,055 --> 00:17:07,092
...redoing everything.
What if they can't leave 20% of the liver?

297
00:17:07,159 --> 00:17:09,461
That's why you'll assist.

298
00:17:09,928 --> 00:17:13,499
You can perfectly handle anything.

299
00:17:13,565 --> 00:17:16,769
Also, you shouldn't go against Mr. Tendo.

300
00:17:17,169 --> 00:17:19,438
He's giving us such a good operation

301
00:17:19,772 --> 00:17:22,875
because he thinks highly of you.

302
00:17:23,409 --> 00:17:24,343
Akira.

303
00:17:25,744 --> 00:17:30,516
- Why take his side now?
- Because you're being childish.

304
00:17:31,750 --> 00:17:32,818
Pong!

305
00:17:37,322 --> 00:17:38,457
Sorry.

306
00:17:47,833 --> 00:17:48,967
Akira.

307
00:17:50,369 --> 00:17:52,638
I've always wanted to ask you.

308
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:57,242
Are you taking my surgery fee?

309
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:04,550
You got money for tomorrow, right?

310
00:18:04,616 --> 00:18:06,285
I didn't hear about that.

311
00:18:11,890 --> 00:18:14,827
Why are you quiet? Explain it to me.

312
00:18:22,734 --> 00:18:24,369
This will get ugly.

313
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:30,742
Let's finish for today.

314
00:18:34,079 --> 00:18:36,248
Michiko. I'm sorry.

315
00:18:39,551 --> 00:18:41,220
So you did steal.

316
00:18:41,653 --> 00:18:42,488
That's not it.

317
00:18:44,189 --> 00:18:45,157
Ron.

318
00:18:46,191 --> 00:18:48,393
Sorry. I won again.

319
00:18:48,827 --> 00:18:50,462
Nine Gates?

320
00:18:51,230 --> 00:18:55,834
Seriously? No way.

321
00:18:55,901 --> 00:18:56,969
Amazing.

322
00:18:59,438 --> 00:19:02,307
Ben Casey, isn't it sad?

323
00:19:02,674 --> 00:19:05,177
A student you carefully trained

324
00:19:05,577 --> 00:19:08,814
is suspecting you of stealing.

325
00:19:13,619 --> 00:19:16,321
The debt from my dad's hospital...

326
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:19,491
I've paid it off, right?

327
00:19:20,926 --> 00:19:23,295
Yes, you did pay back the debt.

328
00:19:24,029 --> 00:19:27,266
But there's no way I'd pocket money.

329
00:19:27,866 --> 00:19:28,834
It's true.

330
00:19:29,902 --> 00:19:34,039
I haven't told you,
but I have a grand plan.

331
00:19:35,274 --> 00:19:36,375
Plan?

332
00:19:36,441 --> 00:19:38,844
So that you can operate all you want,

333
00:19:39,311 --> 00:19:41,046
I'm planning to build

334
00:19:41,113 --> 00:19:43,649
the greatest surgical hospital.

335
00:19:44,049 --> 00:19:45,484
- What?
- In order to do that,

336
00:19:46,151 --> 00:19:49,421
I've been saving the money you made.

337
00:19:50,589 --> 00:19:51,690
I see.

338
00:19:54,393 --> 00:19:55,360
Why not say?

339
00:19:55,427 --> 00:19:56,995
I want good surgeons

340
00:19:57,362 --> 00:19:59,665
to not worry about money

341
00:19:59,731 --> 00:20:04,036
and totally focus on
saving the patient in front of them.

342
00:20:04,803 --> 00:20:07,873
You're the greatest when it comes to that.

343
00:20:09,741 --> 00:20:10,809
Akira...

344
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:18,550
Hey. Which bank is the money in?

345
00:20:19,151 --> 00:20:21,119
Can I see the bankbook?

346
00:20:21,587 --> 00:20:23,555
No, there's no bankbook.

347
00:20:25,557 --> 00:20:29,628
I can't trust banks, so I keep it
in an appropriate place.

348
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:33,131
Don't worry and just focus on surgery.

349
00:20:33,198 --> 00:20:34,700
Right, Ben Casey?

350
00:20:40,806 --> 00:20:44,509
Akira. You think I'm some surgery idiot

351
00:20:45,510 --> 00:20:49,481
who only knows about surgery, don't you?

352
00:20:49,548 --> 00:20:50,482
What?

353
00:20:50,916 --> 00:20:53,919
I might be a surgery idiot.

354
00:20:53,986 --> 00:20:55,354
No, I am.

355
00:20:55,854 --> 00:20:58,357
But I'd never believe that.

356
00:20:58,423 --> 00:21:00,325
- Michiko...
- Liar! Con man!

357
00:21:00,392 --> 00:21:02,995
I'm your teacher.

358
00:21:03,061 --> 00:21:07,366
You're not my teacher anymore.

359
00:21:08,166 --> 00:21:09,368
I was a fool.

360
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,837
Running away? Don't.

361
00:21:11,903 --> 00:21:13,338
You have nowhere to go.

362
00:21:13,405 --> 00:21:15,874
You have surgery tomorrow too.

363
00:21:16,475 --> 00:21:18,277
Don't order me.

364
00:21:40,699 --> 00:21:43,468
Akira was the only one I trusted.

365
00:21:50,575 --> 00:21:51,977
When's the surgery?

366
00:21:52,044 --> 00:21:53,211
- 9AM.
- It's getting cold.

367
00:21:53,278 --> 00:21:54,813
It's very cold

368
00:21:57,482 --> 00:21:58,450
Dr. Kaji.

369
00:22:00,786 --> 00:22:01,887
What's that?

370
00:22:02,487 --> 00:22:03,755
Demon?

371
00:22:12,431 --> 00:22:14,166
Her pulse is stable.

372
00:22:14,232 --> 00:22:15,534
Why's she here?

373
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:17,536
A fight with a guy?

374
00:22:17,602 --> 00:22:19,171
Demon has no man.

375
00:22:19,237 --> 00:22:22,307
She looks pretty cute when she's sleeping.

376
00:22:22,374 --> 00:22:24,409
No way.

377
00:22:29,881 --> 00:22:30,916
You know...

378
00:22:31,416 --> 00:22:34,252
I would've never
expected it, but she's cute.

379
00:22:35,153 --> 00:22:36,121
She's cute.

380
00:22:37,923 --> 00:22:38,824
She's cute.

381
00:22:39,991 --> 00:22:41,226
- So cute.
- She's so cute.

382
00:22:54,306 --> 00:22:55,474
What are you looking at?

383
00:22:58,744 --> 00:23:00,011
Get out.

384
00:23:00,078 --> 00:23:01,713
Don't ever wake up.

385
00:23:02,581 --> 00:23:04,316
I wish she'd sleep forever.

386
00:23:20,999 --> 00:23:23,602
Chief. I have a favor to ask.

387
00:23:23,668 --> 00:23:25,270
- Please
- I'm busy.

388
00:23:32,577 --> 00:23:33,712
What is it?

389
00:23:34,346 --> 00:23:37,015
It's for the surgery.

390
00:23:37,082 --> 00:23:38,717
Ms. Tokachi's?

391
00:23:38,784 --> 00:23:40,051
Just say so.

392
00:23:40,118 --> 00:23:42,187
I will prepare anything you need.

393
00:23:42,888 --> 00:23:43,822
Yes ma'am.

394
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:49,928
You came.

395
00:23:49,995 --> 00:23:50,862
And you?

396
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:54,065
- Hired along with you, as usual.
- I see.

397
00:23:54,533 --> 00:23:55,634
I'm impressed.

398
00:23:56,067 --> 00:23:59,171
You listen to your teacher in the end.

399
00:23:59,237 --> 00:24:00,539
That's not it.

400
00:24:01,139 --> 00:24:02,841
Today's surgery is hard.

401
00:24:03,375 --> 00:24:04,843
He's too sloppy.

402
00:24:04,910 --> 00:24:05,777
I see.

403
00:24:10,682 --> 00:24:12,350
1st assistant.

404
00:24:13,084 --> 00:24:15,086
Make sure you do as I tell you.

405
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:18,423
- It's a world's first, after all.
- Yes, sir.

406
00:24:31,403 --> 00:24:34,673
Good, Michiko. You came.

407
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:43,048
Let's begin.

408
00:24:43,114 --> 00:24:46,751
Ms. Tokachi's myocardial regeneration

409
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:49,287
and liver tumor removal,

410
00:24:49,354 --> 00:24:52,224
using the world's first Fujikawa Method.

411
00:24:53,391 --> 00:24:55,227
First, the heart.

412
00:24:55,293 --> 00:24:56,695
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

413
00:24:56,761 --> 00:24:58,296
Terrible mood.

414
00:24:59,965 --> 00:25:02,634
You're fast and precise
even when you're mad.

415
00:25:03,735 --> 00:25:05,670
Do as I tell you to.

416
00:25:05,737 --> 00:25:06,571
I won't do that.

417
00:25:06,638 --> 00:25:08,640
No median sternotomy.

418
00:25:08,707 --> 00:25:10,842
Do a MIDCAB. Oh, you are.

419
00:25:11,209 --> 00:25:12,577
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

420
00:25:13,812 --> 00:25:17,349
Dr. Fujikawa's doing nothing
and just commentating.

421
00:25:17,749 --> 00:25:19,951
He's making Daimon do it.

422
00:25:20,018 --> 00:25:22,120
I could've done that.

423
00:25:28,527 --> 00:25:31,596
Starting myocardial regeneration.
Autologous myoblast sheet please.

424
00:25:31,663 --> 00:25:32,764
Hold on.

425
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:34,900
That's my job.

426
00:25:35,667 --> 00:25:37,102
Move, 1st assistant.

427
00:25:52,584 --> 00:25:53,585
Perfect.

428
00:25:54,586 --> 00:25:56,154
1st assistant, close her up.

429
00:26:08,333 --> 00:26:10,001
1st assistant, switch.

430
00:26:19,477 --> 00:26:21,880
We'll move to the Fujikawa Method

431
00:26:21,947 --> 00:26:23,748
liver tumor removal.

432
00:26:24,182 --> 00:26:25,383
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

433
00:26:29,688 --> 00:26:32,958
He's making Daimon do it again.

434
00:26:33,024 --> 00:26:35,226
It's mostly Daimon.

435
00:26:35,293 --> 00:26:37,529
Can this be called a world's first?

436
00:26:44,169 --> 00:26:48,373
Remove the liver's whole right lobe
and left lobe S4.

437
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,507
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

438
00:26:49,941 --> 00:26:52,277
Don't damage the veins. Be careful.

439
00:26:55,013 --> 00:26:57,983
SURGERY TIME

440
00:26:58,049 --> 00:27:01,620
She's in hypothermic circulatory arrest.

441
00:27:01,686 --> 00:27:02,520
Yes.

442
00:27:02,587 --> 00:27:04,122
Stopping cardiopulmonary bypass.

443
00:27:04,489 --> 00:27:06,157
Liver's left lobe S4 removal.

444
00:27:19,204 --> 00:27:20,205
What?

445
00:27:20,271 --> 00:27:22,607
Infiltration in S3. Partial resection now.

446
00:27:23,642 --> 00:27:25,577
No. Under 20% of the liver

447
00:27:25,644 --> 00:27:28,013
will remain if you cut more.

448
00:27:28,079 --> 00:27:29,147
- Bipolar.
- Yes.

449
00:27:29,214 --> 00:27:32,317
- No, 1st assistant.
- Shut up.

450
00:27:32,851 --> 00:27:36,154
Body's at 27 degrees.
Five more minutes is the limit. Hurry.

451
00:27:43,428 --> 00:27:45,063
870 grams.

452
00:27:46,398 --> 00:27:48,333
21% remaining.

453
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:49,634
I'll do the veins.

454
00:27:49,701 --> 00:27:51,936
Just as I planned.

455
00:27:53,104 --> 00:27:56,241
We've barely left 20% of the liver.

456
00:27:59,844 --> 00:28:02,113
Done. Hepatic vein next.

457
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:05,183
No, I'll take it from here.

458
00:28:05,250 --> 00:28:08,286
You're done, 1st assistant.

459
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:09,287
Thanks.

460
00:28:09,354 --> 00:28:11,856
He just barges in now.

461
00:28:11,923 --> 00:28:13,625
I could've done that.

462
00:28:16,428 --> 00:28:17,929
6-0 nylon.

463
00:28:17,996 --> 00:28:19,731
- Yes.
- Just move.

464
00:28:19,798 --> 00:28:22,534
That's it for the part-timer. Thanks.

465
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:24,803
- 6-0.
- Move.

466
00:28:25,937 --> 00:28:28,073
I said move.

467
00:28:28,139 --> 00:28:31,342
Leave.

468
00:28:33,678 --> 00:28:36,047
Now, let's get this over with.

469
00:28:43,021 --> 00:28:43,922
VISITOR PASS

470
00:28:43,988 --> 00:28:46,424
It's a one-of-a-kind tie.

471
00:28:46,491 --> 00:28:47,992
Wow!

472
00:28:48,059 --> 00:28:50,028
It's a one-of-a-kind tie.

473
00:28:50,595 --> 00:28:51,563
Thank you.

474
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:57,502
Oh, no.

475
00:28:57,569 --> 00:28:58,803
Is something wrong?

476
00:29:00,038 --> 00:29:00,939
4-0 nylon.

477
00:29:01,806 --> 00:29:02,807
4-0?

478
00:29:02,874 --> 00:29:04,442
Hurry up.

479
00:29:04,909 --> 00:29:05,844
Come on.

480
00:29:06,277 --> 00:29:07,178
Yes.

481
00:29:07,245 --> 00:29:08,146
Scalpel.

482
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:09,481
Yes.

483
00:29:26,631 --> 00:29:28,666
It's over. Good job.

484
00:29:28,733 --> 00:29:30,068
Thank you.

485
00:29:31,503 --> 00:29:36,441
Sir, everything is finished,
just as planned.

486
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:40,678
Thank you.

487
00:29:46,851 --> 00:29:49,320
He's so unfriendly.

488
00:29:50,722 --> 00:29:52,524
NATIONAL ADVANCED MEDICAL CENTER

489
00:30:01,866 --> 00:30:03,301
Please wait a bit longer.

490
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:08,206
We will begin
the press conference by the team

491
00:30:08,273 --> 00:30:11,476
that succeeded
in the world's first Fujikawa Method.

492
00:30:12,544 --> 00:30:13,745
Silence please.

493
00:30:13,812 --> 00:30:17,015
Mr. Tendo, that tie looks great on you.

494
00:30:18,082 --> 00:30:19,918
Dr. Fujikawa!

495
00:30:19,984 --> 00:30:21,152
What?

496
00:30:21,219 --> 00:30:22,387
What is it?

497
00:30:22,453 --> 00:30:25,089
Ms. Tokachi's condition has worsened.

498
00:30:33,631 --> 00:30:34,833
Get the respirator.

499
00:30:34,899 --> 00:30:36,968
- Yes.
- Excuse me.

500
00:30:37,335 --> 00:30:38,369
Coming in. Get ready.

501
00:30:38,937 --> 00:30:42,140
Pale white,
blood pressure 60s, and pulse 130.

502
00:30:42,207 --> 00:30:43,842
A hemorrhagic shock.

503
00:30:43,908 --> 00:30:44,809
Why?

504
00:30:45,443 --> 00:30:47,245
My surgery was perfect.

505
00:30:49,380 --> 00:30:53,518
You must have messed up
when I did the sutures.

506
00:30:54,085 --> 00:30:56,588
I asked for a 6-0 nylon,

507
00:30:57,222 --> 00:30:58,990
but you gave me a thick one.

508
00:31:00,258 --> 00:31:03,161
That's why the suture burst and bled.

509
00:31:03,228 --> 00:31:05,296
No,

510
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:08,499
- you said 4-0 nylon...
- I would never say such a thing.

511
00:31:09,100 --> 00:31:10,034
That's it.

512
00:31:10,602 --> 00:31:12,704
That's why there's hemorrhaging.

513
00:31:12,770 --> 00:31:14,272
It's your fault.

514
00:31:14,939 --> 00:31:16,507
What have you done?

515
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:28,853
Michiko.

516
00:31:30,822 --> 00:31:32,223
I know you're there.

517
00:31:33,925 --> 00:31:38,463
Because you didn't finish up,
that patient might die.

518
00:31:40,265 --> 00:31:43,368
Dr. Fujikawa made sloppy sutures

519
00:31:43,434 --> 00:31:45,303
and the patient's critical.

520
00:31:45,803 --> 00:31:50,375
On top of that,
it seems like it's Chief Shiraki's fault.

521
00:31:51,943 --> 00:31:57,582
Due to the Chief's mistake,
the hepatic vein's suture ripped.

522
00:31:57,649 --> 00:32:00,451
Of all things,

523
00:32:00,518 --> 00:32:02,820
she handed me the wrong suture.

524
00:32:03,288 --> 00:32:04,789
I'm terribly sorry.

525
00:32:05,390 --> 00:32:08,593
The surgery and the manuscript are ruined.

526
00:32:08,660 --> 00:32:11,963
You ruined the greatest chance

527
00:32:12,730 --> 00:32:14,565
with the worst mistake.

528
00:32:14,632 --> 00:32:17,235
No, this was her fault.

529
00:32:17,302 --> 00:32:18,469
As a result,

530
00:32:19,871 --> 00:32:21,906
not only will this not be publicized,

531
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:24,876
it won't be
a world's first clinical report.

532
00:32:26,044 --> 00:32:28,079
And this hospital's honor...

533
00:32:31,082 --> 00:32:32,617
You defamed it.

534
00:32:32,684 --> 00:32:34,052
I will make up for this.

535
00:32:35,019 --> 00:32:36,888
I'll remove half the remaining liver

536
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:39,791
and operate again to restore it.

537
00:32:49,367 --> 00:32:54,605
I will take full responsibility
for what happened.

538
00:32:55,073 --> 00:32:57,608
- Ms. Shiraki...
- It's to protect the hospital's honor.

539
00:33:00,812 --> 00:33:06,217
And yours.

540
00:33:06,284 --> 00:33:07,151
RESIGNATION

541
00:33:09,120 --> 00:33:10,655
I cannot accept this.

542
00:33:12,190 --> 00:33:14,192
Another surgery to save the patient

543
00:33:15,293 --> 00:33:17,962
is the priority right now.

544
00:33:27,672 --> 00:33:30,541
Chief,
bring me what I asked for this morning.

545
00:33:30,875 --> 00:33:31,776
Hurry!

546
00:33:32,910 --> 00:33:35,513
IN SURGERY

547
00:33:35,947 --> 00:33:38,349
No wonder it smells weird.

548
00:33:38,416 --> 00:33:40,118
The old lady's here.

549
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:42,253
How irritating. Have Aya do it.

550
00:33:42,653 --> 00:33:44,622
This is your fault.

551
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:48,192
You ruined the surgery
and clinical report.

552
00:33:48,259 --> 00:33:49,093
Get out.

553
00:33:49,527 --> 00:33:52,330
Just move and have Aya do it.

554
00:33:56,734 --> 00:33:57,869
Let's start.

555
00:33:57,935 --> 00:33:59,203
- Remover.
- Yes.

556
00:34:08,579 --> 00:34:09,414
Move.

557
00:34:10,782 --> 00:34:11,716
Remover.

558
00:34:22,093 --> 00:34:23,194
This is terrible.

559
00:34:23,261 --> 00:34:24,962
You're too sloppy.

560
00:34:25,029 --> 00:34:26,931
Of course it'll burst

561
00:34:26,998 --> 00:34:28,833
with such thick sutures.

562
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:31,969
This liver can't regenerate anyway.

563
00:34:32,036 --> 00:34:34,338
Everything is ruined

564
00:34:34,405 --> 00:34:35,640
thanks to this old hag.

565
00:34:35,706 --> 00:34:37,575
I'll regenerate the liver.

566
00:34:38,342 --> 00:34:40,011
You think you're god?

567
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:42,413
Only 15% is left.

568
00:34:42,480 --> 00:34:43,815
Chief, please.

569
00:34:43,881 --> 00:34:45,383
- Yes.
- What?

570
00:34:45,450 --> 00:34:48,686
Autologous bone marrow cell.

571
00:34:48,753 --> 00:34:49,887
Please prepare.

572
00:34:49,954 --> 00:34:51,222
- Ms. Yagami, please.
- Yes.

573
00:34:51,856 --> 00:34:53,291
Hold on.

574
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:56,294
- You can regenerate the liver?
- You didn't know?

575
00:34:57,061 --> 00:34:59,597
I'll remove the necrotic parts.

576
00:34:59,664 --> 00:35:00,898
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

577
00:35:00,965 --> 00:35:03,000
- Wait...
- Ms. Tokachi's charts had

578
00:35:03,067 --> 00:35:05,703
bone marrow cell culturing recorded.

579
00:35:05,770 --> 00:35:06,838
I'm sure.

580
00:35:06,904 --> 00:35:07,972
Why not tell me?

581
00:35:08,039 --> 00:35:10,374
I thought you knew.

582
00:35:10,441 --> 00:35:12,009
Hold on.

583
00:35:12,643 --> 00:35:16,114
Isn't this...A world's first?

584
00:35:16,547 --> 00:35:19,917
A huge one at that.

585
00:35:19,984 --> 00:35:23,287
Ms. Daimon, you're my savior.

586
00:35:23,821 --> 00:35:24,822
Good luck.

587
00:35:24,889 --> 00:35:26,924
Shut up.

588
00:35:41,072 --> 00:35:43,641
Administering autologous
bone marrow cell culture.

589
00:36:12,236 --> 00:36:13,604
Thank you.

590
00:36:24,215 --> 00:36:27,385
RESIGNATION

591
00:36:40,598 --> 00:36:42,400
Dr. Daimon, thank you.

592
00:36:45,303 --> 00:36:49,640
It was short,
but thank you for everything.

593
00:36:51,509 --> 00:36:52,476
What do you mean?

594
00:36:53,678 --> 00:36:54,745
The second surgery

595
00:36:55,746 --> 00:36:57,982
was a success thanks to you,

596
00:36:59,784 --> 00:37:03,854
but I will take responsibility
for the first surgery

597
00:37:04,922 --> 00:37:05,890
and quit.

598
00:37:05,957 --> 00:37:07,491
You're fine with that?

599
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:13,397
It's to protect this hospital.

600
00:37:14,665 --> 00:37:17,768
If the Medical Care Center is defamed,

601
00:37:18,669 --> 00:37:21,239
it means Mr. Tendo will be as well.

602
00:37:21,305 --> 00:37:22,173
What?

603
00:37:24,242 --> 00:37:26,978
So you really love Tendo.

604
00:37:27,612 --> 00:37:29,046
I'm not worthy.

605
00:37:29,113 --> 00:37:32,383
I won't say anything about your type...

606
00:37:33,351 --> 00:37:34,652
But if you quit,

607
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:37,355
what will happen to your juniors?

608
00:37:40,124 --> 00:37:42,927
If you take the blame
for Fujikawa's mistake,

609
00:37:44,528 --> 00:37:47,632
wouldn't it hurt the pride of all nurses?

610
00:37:52,436 --> 00:37:53,771
I've made up my mind.

611
00:38:04,048 --> 00:38:05,483
NATIONAL ADVANCED MEDICAL CENTER

612
00:38:05,549 --> 00:38:07,551
Please tell Dr. Fujikawa to come

613
00:38:07,885 --> 00:38:10,054
to the president's room later.

614
00:38:10,121 --> 00:38:12,657
Both directors won't come yet.

615
00:38:13,057 --> 00:38:13,891
I see.

616
00:38:18,362 --> 00:38:20,398
No, don't, don't.

617
00:38:20,998 --> 00:38:24,902
Oh, no...Don't...

618
00:38:25,836 --> 00:38:27,271
I'm so sleepy.

619
00:38:31,909 --> 00:38:36,380
JUNKO SHIRAKI

620
00:38:50,394 --> 00:38:54,231
Chief, here. A farewell gift.

621
00:38:56,067 --> 00:38:59,303
If you want, I'll even find you a new job.

622
00:38:59,870 --> 00:39:03,307
So just keep your mouth shut.

623
00:39:03,374 --> 00:39:04,975
I cannot.

624
00:39:05,042 --> 00:39:06,911
It's just to show my gratitude.

625
00:39:06,977 --> 00:39:08,446
Take it.

626
00:39:09,714 --> 00:39:12,416
The heavens will get mad.

627
00:39:14,051 --> 00:39:15,653
I'm sorry, Director Fujikawa...

628
00:39:16,721 --> 00:39:18,889
This is a national medical center.

629
00:39:19,924 --> 00:39:24,161
I am a government worker
at this national hospital.

630
00:39:24,228 --> 00:39:26,364
You are also a government worker

631
00:39:27,098 --> 00:39:29,133
as a doctor of a national hospital.

632
00:39:30,201 --> 00:39:31,068
So what?

633
00:39:31,135 --> 00:39:32,536
A person like me

634
00:39:33,371 --> 00:39:34,872
cannot receive money

635
00:39:34,939 --> 00:39:37,108
from a person like you.

636
00:39:37,174 --> 00:39:39,877
Don't be so stubborn.

637
00:39:40,244 --> 00:39:42,012
All the doctors here secretly

638
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:44,949
get money from the patients.

639
00:39:45,015 --> 00:39:46,584
No!

640
00:39:51,689 --> 00:39:53,858
This money is like admitting

641
00:39:53,924 --> 00:39:58,329
that you made a surgical error
and blamed it on me.

642
00:40:07,738 --> 00:40:09,039
Chief Shiraki.

643
00:40:09,106 --> 00:40:11,175
Chief...

644
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:12,276
Chief,

645
00:40:12,343 --> 00:40:16,046
please don't quit.

646
00:40:18,649 --> 00:40:19,617
You guys...

647
00:40:30,261 --> 00:40:31,128
Chief.

648
00:40:34,031 --> 00:40:34,932
Hey.

649
00:40:36,434 --> 00:40:38,102
You missed one.

650
00:40:51,816 --> 00:40:53,717
Chief,

651
00:40:53,784 --> 00:40:55,052
please don't quit.

652
00:40:55,119 --> 00:40:56,287
Don't quit.

653
00:40:56,687 --> 00:40:58,789
Please...

654
00:40:59,223 --> 00:41:03,093
You'll be able to return to
work by the end of the month,

655
00:41:04,028 --> 00:41:05,963
Soon-to-be Minister.

656
00:41:08,933 --> 00:41:10,868
You saved my life...

657
00:41:11,802 --> 00:41:14,271
I will surely establish

658
00:41:15,606 --> 00:41:17,842
the Japan Healthcare Organization.

659
00:41:19,577 --> 00:41:22,246
I'll put my career on the line.

660
00:41:22,580 --> 00:41:24,415
Thank you.

661
00:41:34,158 --> 00:41:36,827
- Thank you.
- 6-0 nylon.

662
00:41:37,561 --> 00:41:39,563
I said move.

663
00:41:39,630 --> 00:41:40,598
Move.

664
00:41:41,732 --> 00:41:42,600
Move aside.

665
00:41:45,436 --> 00:41:46,971
Sir, he's here.

666
00:41:48,072 --> 00:41:49,740
You called for me?

667
00:41:49,807 --> 00:41:52,109
Ms. Tokachi's doing great

668
00:41:52,176 --> 00:41:53,511
after the second operation.

669
00:41:53,577 --> 00:41:56,580
You made a mistake the first time

670
00:41:56,647 --> 00:41:59,083
because of something like this?

671
00:42:12,630 --> 00:42:14,031
Oh no...

672
00:42:14,098 --> 00:42:15,099
Something wrong?

673
00:42:15,165 --> 00:42:16,166
4-0 nylon.

674
00:42:16,233 --> 00:42:17,268
4-0?

675
00:42:17,701 --> 00:42:18,836
Hurry up.

676
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:20,037
Yes.

677
00:42:25,075 --> 00:42:29,013
There were two one-of-a-kind ties.

678
00:42:31,782 --> 00:42:34,251
Sir, he's here again.

679
00:42:34,318 --> 00:42:35,786
Hello.

680
00:42:38,422 --> 00:42:41,358
I just realized

681
00:42:41,825 --> 00:42:43,961
the tie from Director Fujikawa

682
00:42:44,828 --> 00:42:48,432
was the same as Mr. Tendo's. I'm honored.

683
00:42:48,499 --> 00:42:51,936
But I guess it wasn't one-of-a-kind.

684
00:42:53,737 --> 00:42:55,039
Excuse me.

685
00:43:06,317 --> 00:43:07,451
This is a melon.

686
00:43:11,589 --> 00:43:13,057
This is a bill.

687
00:43:13,123 --> 00:43:15,993
Thank you once again.

688
00:43:16,560 --> 00:43:19,797
This time, 1st Assistant Daimon

689
00:43:20,331 --> 00:43:23,867
succeeded in
a world's first clinical report.

690
00:43:24,568 --> 00:43:27,037
She covered for Dr. Fujikawa's mistake,

691
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:31,609
and saved the next Minister
of Health, Labor and Welfare.

692
00:43:33,978 --> 00:43:36,413
44 MILLION

693
00:43:36,480 --> 00:43:38,649
The highest price yet.

694
00:43:39,049 --> 00:43:41,385
I subtracted the deposit money.

695
00:43:41,452 --> 00:43:42,653
Very well.

696
00:43:43,354 --> 00:43:46,457
As usual, we will wire the money to you.

697
00:43:46,523 --> 00:43:48,892
I'm happy that we could be of help.

698
00:43:49,560 --> 00:43:53,364
Please accept the melon today.

699
00:43:55,099 --> 00:43:59,670
It's a bit late,
but it's a birthday present.

700
00:44:00,904 --> 00:44:02,573
Happy birthday.

701
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:04,475
Well, well...

702
00:44:06,143 --> 00:44:09,346
Then I shall accept it just this once.

703
00:44:19,556 --> 00:44:21,358
I'm home.

704
00:44:24,695 --> 00:44:29,166
I have nowhere to go...

705
00:44:29,233 --> 00:44:31,669
So I came back, Akira!

706
00:44:33,804 --> 00:44:34,905
Akira?

707
00:44:37,841 --> 00:44:39,410
Akira?

708
00:44:43,213 --> 00:44:48,719
Ben Casey. Where's Akira?

709
00:44:49,920 --> 00:44:51,522
Akira...

710
00:44:52,823 --> 00:44:55,693
The highest price ever!

711
00:44:56,226 --> 00:44:58,429
I'll have to celebrate tonight.

712
00:44:58,495 --> 00:45:01,999
Michiko should just hurry on home.

713
00:45:25,355 --> 00:45:28,025
I wonder what Akira's doing.

714
00:45:28,826 --> 00:45:32,996
I even bought
taiyaki pastries for him too.

715
00:45:38,235 --> 00:45:40,804
You're late... It's cold.

716
00:45:45,109 --> 00:45:46,610
I'll borrow this.

717
00:45:48,746 --> 00:45:50,881
It's cold, Ben Casey.

718
00:45:53,250 --> 00:45:56,854
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

719
00:45:57,321 --> 00:46:01,558
<i>Her medical license</i>
<i>and experience are her only weapons.</i>

720
00:46:03,026 --> 00:46:06,396
THANK YOU, MICHIKO

721
00:46:13,137 --> 00:46:14,838
He's late.

722
00:46:15,506 --> 00:46:20,611
Your taiyaki is getting cold, Akira.

723
00:46:25,082 --> 00:46:27,317
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

724
00:46:28,252 --> 00:46:31,522
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

725
00:46:34,124 --> 00:46:35,592
FINAL EPISODE

726
00:46:35,659 --> 00:46:38,629
I want to operate
on the one person I love.

727
00:46:39,062 --> 00:46:40,964
Long time no see.

728
00:46:41,031 --> 00:46:42,299
Please save me.

729
00:46:42,366 --> 00:46:44,268
So it's over with you?

730
00:46:44,334 --> 00:46:45,335
Yes.

731
00:46:45,402 --> 00:46:49,006
I cannot let Michiko Daimon fail.
